@PalantirTech and Armada said on October 1, 2026, that they will offer sovereign AI on modular data centers built in the United States and allied countries, and that Palantir is naming Armada its inaugural certified modular data-center partner, the companies said in a Business Wire release.

Palantir will validate its Sovereign AI Operating System — AIP, Ontology, Foundry, and Apollo — on Armada’s Galleon hardware, with the Armada Platform and Sovereign AI Grid for control across sites. Customers are meant to run and adapt open-weight models, including NVIDIA Nemotron, on infrastructure they own, including fully air-gapped deployments. Chief executive Alex Karp said the point is owning the weights, the data, and the hardware, and getting that hardware in months rather than years.

Why it matters: named Palantir partnership with a concrete hardware partner and an air-gap claim — irreversible Peak B FACT unused this week. Sources: Palantir / Armada / Business Wire, 1 Oct 2026.

